{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790527824,"nonce":"FTP+Cjo5p0aQxjAkTXooSxCp3sI=","title":"caribou serve: hot-reload spoke modules in the running page","message":"When a Wren (or Zyntax-frontend) module under a served project changes, caribou serve compiles only that module to a wasm side module and hands it to the page; the running program loads it and runs World::reload for it, keeping program state (classes keep identity, objects get the new bodies, call sites refill). A Haxe entry or plugin change still rebuilds and reloads the page. The program hears of the change through the world's watched word (sched::watch) or a host import. Needs: Ash's browser host loading a side module into a running program (today ash_host_dlopen answers 0 in a page; side modules load only in the native host, before start), and WrenLift reloading a module from compiled code rather than source (no interpreters on AOT/wasm). Part of the dev server, git-bug 8943d6f000493cea4cadb5cd026fd0ae5299bfe6ce61d146d0420f4471593dce.","files":null}]}